I implemented the node itself but left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access, and the metadata fetch would need `aap:caps/http-client`. Neither is granted, and the node shouldn't reach for authority it wasn't given. Sending the input's text to an external URL would also be a data leak. If operations needs these, the graph author should add the capabilities to the node's `with` clause, and then they can be implemented.

The node marks each considered id as seen in the store, but only when the digest was actually published. If it wasn't published, nothing is recorded, so those items can be retried next run. `recorded` is the number of ids written.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            for id in &published.considered {
                state_rw::put(id, "1");
                recorded += 1;
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

